            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4"
          ],
          "text": "On admission, blood glucose was 'HI' on BM with blood ketones 5.2, pH 7.18, bicarbonate 11 and glucose 34. She was managed on the ward HDU with PICU informed, and treated with cautious IV fluids, fixed-rate insulin infusion, potassium replacement and hourly monitoring per DKA protocol. By Day 2, pH had improved to 7.34 and ketones to 0.8. She was transitioned to subcutaneous insulin on a basal-bolus regimen. Diabetes nurse and dietician input commenced, with family education covering carbohydrate counting, hypo management and sick-day rules.",
