    "compose_patient": {
      "sections": [
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "Your child came in because she had been:\n- drinking and weeing much more than usual for 2 weeks\n- losing weight\n- vomiting, having tummy pain and feeling drowsy for 2 days\n\nThe team found that your child has type 1 diabetes. She also had a serious complication of diabetes called diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA). This was a new diagnosis."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team did blood tests. These showed high blood sugar and high ketones, and that her blood had become too acidic. By Day 2, the tests showed the acidosis was getting better.\n\nYour child was cared for in the high-dependency area of the ward. The team looking after the intensive care unit was also informed.\n\nShe was treated with:\n- fluids given through a drip\n- insulin given through a drip\n- potassium replacement through the drip\n- checks every hour\n\nOn Day 2, she moved on to insulin given by injection under the skin (a basal-bolus regimen).\n\nThe diabetes nurse and dietician started working with your child and your family. Education began, including carbohydrate counting, how to manage low blood sugar, and what to do when your child is unwell."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7",
            "sections.8"
          ],
          "text": "- The diabetes team will follow up in 1 week.\n- Phone support is available in the time before that appointment.\n- A dietician follow-up has been arranged.\n- Your child's GP has been made aware. No urgent action is needed from the GP at this time."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.4",
